{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793743040,"nonce":"ELBwr7CKQ594NHP5fVkdiu5Ap9Y=","message":"Landing deployment planning, 2026-11-03: user confirmed normal Ashui previews render on the session host and stream graphics; the landing demo alone can use precompiled cached WASM. Keep this host-rendering work relevant to ordinary workspace sessions, without blocking the landing demo.\n\nSoftware rendering candidates: Mesa Lavapipe for the native Linux Vulkan/wgpu path, Mesa llvmpipe for OpenGL frameworks, SwiftShader as an alternative Vulkan CPU implementation. xgpu native Linux uses the installed Vulkan ICD; it does not bundle a vendor/software driver. Ashui Offscreen.create requests HighPerformance and currently has no explicit fallback selection. Availability and compatibility must be established with a real bounded MSB guest test, not inferred from software Vulkan support. No need for GPU passthrough if the software ICD works; KVM is still required for the chosen VM isolation backend.\n\nBenchmark the real surface path on the NUC with no hardware render device: load app, read first frame, click/type/resize and verify output, then exercise idle/hidden/closed. Record renderer identity, cold/warm first frame, CPU, peak/resident RAM, bytes on the actual gateway relay, input latency and visual fidelity. Compare software to hardware only where hardware is actually accessible. Existing dynASB Linux/Venus claims remain unverified until their separate bring-up passes.\n\nDo not promise cheaper hosting just from avoiding a GPU. SurfacePreview currently grants 60 credits/s; the shim performs full render/readback before SurfaceLink suppresses unchanged output. SurfaceLink has an optional deflate flag but the Ashui shim leaves it false. Process output is chunked at 16 KiB and base64 wrapped in JSON; measure that request/CPU/transfer amplification through the Cloudflare DO as well. Prefer invalidation-driven idle rendering and bounded dirty-rectangle lossless transport for the mostly-static board before selecting video encoding for every UI. Preserve text sharpness and the tested fractional-DPR sizing; any resolution/frame-rate policy must be explicit.\n\nPrimary references checked:\nhttps://docs.mesa3d.org/sourcetree.html (Lavapipe software Vulkan frontend)\nhttps://docs.mesa3d.org/drivers/llvmpipe.html\nhttps://swiftshader.googlesource.com/SwiftShader/+/HEAD/README.md","files":null}]}